All four files are complete and parse cleanly. Final report:

## Files created/edited

- **EDIT** `SwiftMandarin/Services/CloudAIService.swift` — additive only: `chatTurns(...)` + two private static body builders (`openAIBodyTurns`, `anthropicBodyTurns`). No existing method changed. Reuses `buildURL`/`applyAuthHeaders`/`parseOpenAIContent`/`parseAnthropicContent`; replicates `openAIBody`'s temperature rules (reasoning-model `max_completion_tokens` for o-series, plain `max_tokens` for other reasoners, Kimi temperature exception via `allowsCustomTemperature: provider != .kimi`), JSON prompt hint, and `response_format` only where `supportsJSONResponseFormat`.
- **NEW** `SwiftMandarin/Services/ConversationService.swift`
- **NEW** `SwiftMandarin/Models/ConversationStore.swift`
- **NEW** `SwiftMandarin/Views/ConversationView.swift`

## Public API exposed

```swift
// CloudAIService (added)
func chatTurns(provider: AIProvider, model: String, system: String,
               turns: [(role: String, content: String)],
               jsonMode: Bool = false, maxTokens: Int = 2048) async throws -> String

// ConversationService.swift
enum ConversationScenario: String, CaseIterable, Codable, Identifiable, Sendable
    // cases: freeChat, cafe, directions, shopping, introductions, travel, doctor
    // members: var symbolName: String; var titleKey: String; var descriptionKey: String; var sceneSeed: String
struct PartnerReply: Codable, Sendable { var reply: String; var pinyin: String?; var translation: String; var feedback: String? }
@MainActor final class ConversationService {
    static let shared: ConversationService
    func reply(scenario: ConversationScenario, history: [ConversationMessage], learningIsChinese: Bool) async throws -> PartnerReply
}

// ConversationStore.swift
struct ConversationMessage: Codable, Identifiable, Hashable, Sendable
    // init(id: UUID = UUID(), isUser: Bool, text: String, pinyin: String? = nil, translation: String? = nil, feedback: String? = nil, date: Date = Date())
struct Conversation: Codable, Identifiable, Hashable, Sendable
    // id, scenario, messages, dateStarted, dateUpdated (tolerant decodes; unknown scenario → .freeChat)
@Observable @MainActor final class ConversationStore {
    static let shared: ConversationStore
    private(set) var conversations: [Conversation]                    // newest-updated first, capped at 50
    func conversation(withID id: UUID) -> Conversation?
    @discardableResult func startConversation(scenario: ConversationScenario) -> Conversation
    func append(message: ConversationMessage, to conversationID: UUID)
    func attachFeedback(_ feedback: String, toMessageID messageID: UUID, in conversationID: UUID)
    func remove(_ conversation: Conversation)
}

// ConversationView.swift
struct ConversationView: View   // self-contained NavigationStack
```

## Design decisions

- **Feedback lives on the learner's message** (`ConversationMessage.feedback`, set via `attachFeedback`), so the orange lightbulb banner renders directly under the bubble it corrects; `PartnerReply.feedback` is routed there when the reply lands.
- **Anthropic turn constraints**: the greeting call has no user turn and history starts with the assistant greeting, so `ConversationService` inserts synthetic user cue turns (first-message-must-be-user, request-must-end-on-user); harmless for OpenAI-style providers.
- **Graceful parse degradation**: tolerant `extractJSONObject` + tolerant `PartnerReply` decode; unparseable responses fall back to fence-stripped raw text as the reply. Missing pinyin for a Chinese reply is derived locally via `PinyinConverter.convert`; pinyin is force-nilled for English replies (bilingual parity — never native furniture in 中文 UI). Pinyin toolbar toggle only appears when `learningIsChinese`, default on.
- **`SpeechRecognitionService` has a `private init` singleton** (contract said instantiate, but the actual file forbids it) — I follow the existing `LiveSpeechTranslationView` pattern: `@State private var speech = SpeechRecognitionService.shared`, observing `completeTranscript` (no delegate; no existing code conforms to the delegate either). A `micSessionActive` flag plus `micBaseline` prevents stray transcripts and preserves typed text. Mic works on both platforms (service is cross-platform). Pulsing red mic while recording.
- **Store persistence** copies `WordExplanationCacheStore`'s coalesced single-writer atomic off-main file write (2s throttle, `conversations.json` in Application Support).
- **Greeting race guard**: re-entering the chat while the first greeting request is in flight can't produce a duplicate greeting.
- No sheets/popovers are presented, so no `.localizedSurface()` sites were needed. Error banner is dismissible with Retry (re-runs `reply()` on current history without duplicating the user message).

## New user-facing English string literals (for the central localization pass)

"Conversation", "Practice speaking with an AI partner", "Pick a scene and chat by voice or text. Your partner replies in the language you're learning and gently corrects your mistakes.", "New conversation", "Continue", "Delete", "No messages yet", "Free chat", "At the café", "Directions", "Shopping", "Introductions", "Travel", "At the doctor", "Chat about anything", "Order drinks and snacks", "Find your way around town", "Ask prices and haggle", "Meet someone new", "Airports, hotels, and tickets", "Describe how you feel", "Show pinyin", "Translation", "Message", "Retry", "Dismiss", "Send", "Dictate", "Stop recording", "Play audio", "Partner is typing"

Reused existing key (not new): "No AI provider is configured. Add one in Settings → AI (or run a local Ollama server)." — via `String(localized:)`, identical to `WordIdentificationService`. The toolbar label "拼音" uses `Text(verbatim:)` deliberately (it only appears in the English UI as a learning aid) and must NOT be added to the catalog.

